cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "corestone: fracture-controlled chemical weathering of granite"
abstract: >-
  Evolves a two-dimensional vertical cross section of jointed granite as
  infiltrating water dissolves it along a seeded fracture network. Mineral
  dissolution follows an Arrhenius rate constant modulated by the chemical
  affinity of the pore fluid, so weathering rate depends on how far the water
  is from saturation as well as on temperature. The differential reactivity of
  plagioclase, biotite and K-feldspar disaggregates the rock into grus where
  water reaches it, leaving unaltered corestones where it does not.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Wickert
    given-names: Andrew D.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9545-3365"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/MNiMORPH/corestone"
keywords:
